Well I was a little underwhelmed and the *nil* response to my previous query 
concerning the IBM version of Nethack 3.09 (got it via FTP from linc). Please, 
if anyone can shed any light on this re-occuring problem, send a reply.

I've had numerous great NetHack 3.09 sessions ruined when I accidentally hit 
the '!' key at the command level. This correctly does a shell to DOS
(MS-DOS v3.3). I can issue normal DOS commands (ie: dir, copy, etc) just fine. 
But then when I enter "exit" in order to get back into the game, the computer 
clears the screen, puts a funny non-alpha character in the upper left corner 
of the screen, and then dies. No keys are recognized. No way to save the game. 
It's off in never-never land. I have to Ctrl-Alt-Del or Reset to get the 
computer back. When I get back into my NetHack directory, I of course see all 
the LEVELS.* files from my previous session, but the character is gone. 
My current policy is to restore my save file from the last copy I made, 
but that could have been lots of hours previously (when I'm going good).

Has anyone ever encountered this problem? Solved it? Has anyone with the
IBM version done a shell escape and actually gotten back to their game?
If so, please let me know what version of DOS, maybe a copy of your 
CONFIG.SYS and AUTOEXEC.BAT files so that I can figure what it is about
my setup/environment is causing my problem.

I should say that I can sucessfully shell to DOS from most other programs
(ie: Telix, ProComm, DF, etc) and from those I write in Turbo Pascal.
No problem shelling to DOS, issue whatever commands, and then exit to return
back to the original program. The problem seems to be peculiar to NetHack.
I also had this same problem with older versions of PC-HACK 3.61 (and earlier)
from Don Kneller. So this problem has been with me for quite some time.

Need help here. Thanks.

